 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to establishing a\nnative plant seed supply, development and enhancement program",
    "basePrintNo": "S7849",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7849-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §142-b, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7849\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to estab-\nlishing a native plant seed supply, development and enhancement program\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo establish the New York native plant seed supply, development, and\nenhancement program, increasing the availability and use of native plant\nseeds across the state\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 introduces the program, providing definitions and assigning\noversight to relevant institutions.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date of the bill\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe insufficient supply of native plant seeds presents a formidable\nobstacle to crucial ecological restoration and revegetation projects.\nNative plants play a pivotal role in maintaining biodiversity, partic-\nularly in areas affected by extreme events, invasive plants, and other\nhazards. The current inadequacy of native seed supply leads to the\nsubstitution of nonnative varieties or seeds sourced from different\nregions, compromising restoration efforts.\n\nThis bill aligns New York with recommendations from the 2023 report by\nthe National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine (\"An\nAssessment of Native Seed Needs and the Capacity for Their Supply\") and\nwill contribute to a national effort to address challenges posed by\nclimate change. This bill would make these seeds more accessible,\nrequire the state to use native seeds whenever possible and practicable,\nand encourage citizens to do the same.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
